# Maintainer batch 20260824-051848. NO ROWS, NO QUEUE ENTRIES. One program repair
# landed directly (pod.py, not this proposal's own scope -- see below).
#
# LJ-1.541 and LJ-1.572: same two `attempt_max:sys-timeout-escalate` parks carried
# across every batch since 20260824-005804, unchanged. Settled by direct
# correspondence with the resident mathematician: leave both parked, no state
# write, no row, no retry. Nothing new to propose.
#
# LJ-1.603: reason `row:task-lj-1-603-heap-wall-park`, exit_code 251, error_class
# heap_wall, 32 changed files (all its own). NO ROW AND NO QUEUE ENTRY. This is
# `task-lj-1-603-heap-wall-park` doing exactly what maintainer-backlog item 26
# asked of it: `action = "park"` instead of a looping `escalate`, so this parks
# ONCE instead of repeating to `attempt_max`. THE SHADOWING LIST entry ("row
# sys-heap-wall lost 1 time(s)") is AD8 working as designed -- the task-scoped
# row outranks the system one by construction, and here the task-scoped row is
# the CORRECTED template, so losing to it is the right outcome, not a defect.
#
# ONE REAL DEFECT FOUND WHILE READING THIS PARK, REPAIRED DIRECTLY IN THE
# PROGRAM (scripts/pod/pod.py, outside this proposal's SCOPE, so it is reported
# here and not written as a row): `_rule_a2()`'s B2 anti-loop guard
# (`pod.py:~4295`, before the fix) only recognised a stored park reason spelled
# `"attempt_max:" + row_id`. A plain `park` action (and `park_and_split`) writes
# its reason as `"row:" + row_id` (`emit_park()`, `pod.py:4067`), a DIFFERENT
# spelling the guard never matched. Concretely: the very next unrelated
# `table.toml` write -- ANY `expire_rows()` firing on ANY other task's row, or
# any other batch landing one row for something else -- would have bumped
# `mtime` past `[LJ-1.603]`'s `parked_at`, re-routed its stored record to the
# SAME `task-lj-1-603-heap-wall-park` row (nothing about the row changed), found
# `"row:task-lj-1-603-heap-wall-park" != "attempt_max:task-lj-1-603-heap-wall-
# park"`, and reopened it to READY anyway -- a second dispatch straight back
# into the same heap wall for no reason at all. Fixed: the guard now checks
# both spellings. New regression test in `scripts/tests/test_pod_loop.py`
# (`test_a_PLAIN_park_row_ALSO_stays_while_the_guilty_row_still_wins`) reproduces
# the LJ-1.603 shape directly. All four pod suites, check-spec-surface and
# lint-prose ran clean after the fix.

[batch]
ts = "20260824-051848"
rows_proposed = 0
reason = "No table row and no queue entry for any of the three. LJ-1.541/572 unchanged, settled with the mathematician (leave parked). LJ-1.603's heap-wall park is the corrected task-scoped template (backlog item 26) working as designed; its shadowing of sys-heap-wall is AD8, not a defect. Found and fixed directly in the program (outside this proposal's scope): _rule_a2()'s B2 anti-loop guard did not recognise a plain park action's own reason spelling ('row:' + row_id, only 'attempt_max:' + row_id was checked), which would have let the next unrelated table.toml write reopen LJ-1.603 into the same heap wall. New regression test added; all suites and gates clean."
